    "executiveSummary": "Imagine popping the hood of a running car to see exactly how fuel, ignition, and pistons convert raw energy into motion. Most meditation guides focus merely on calming down, like turning down the dashboard radio. Bhikkhu An\u0101layo's rigorous analysis of the fourth foundation\u2014the Contemplation of Dhamma\u2014examines the actual mechanical transmission. Instead of getting tangled in the narrative content of your thoughts, you learn to observe the universal operating rules of mental phenomena: how states ignite, how they feed on cognitive inputs, and how they starve when denied attention.\n\nThe genius of this fourth layer is its diagnostic precision. It treats human psychological patterns like an engineer troubleshooting a complex electrical grid. First, you detect system drags\u2014sloth, irritability, second-guessing\u2014the mental equivalents of friction in a wheel bearing. Next, you disassemble identity itself into modular components: sensory inputs, visceral feeling tones, reflexive labeling, and behavioral impulses. You discover that what you call 'myself' is actually a decentralized network of rapid subprocesses, none of which holds permanent authority.\n\nFinally, the practice shifts from passive monitoring to deliberate system tuning. By identifying which conditions spark mental clarity and which spark tension, you run precise feedback loops. Just as an Olympic rowing crew synchronizes power and balance to glide effortlessly across choppy water, you train attention, curiosity, energy, and equanimity to work together. The ultimate payoff is not temporary quietness, but permanent psychological freedom built on a clear-eyed understanding of cause and effect.",
