      "keyInsight": "Most people treat personal growth like climbing Mount Everest with heavy packs. They assume you need extreme rituals, rare states of trance, or complex philosophies. The direct path turns this completely upside down. It works more like opening a clear window in a dusty room. You do not have to invent fresh states of mind. You simply watch what is already happening right here. The paradox is startling. By dropping the exhausting hunt for special experiences, clarity appears instantly. We waste decades looking for secret shortcuts when our direct experience was sitting right in front of us.",
