      "headline": "Sati: The Guard at the City Gate",
      "keyInsight": "People think of mindfulness as a soft, dreamy cloud where everything feels warm and fuzzy. In truth, authentic awareness works like a seasoned security guard standing at a bustling city gate. It does not wrestle every visitor to the ground. It simply spots who is walking into town. Is it an honest fruit vendor or a sneaky thief? Awareness notices an incoming impulse before that impulse hijacks your steering wheel. The paradox is immense. You do not gain control by using brutal willpower. You gain total control by simply remembering to look.",
